The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```c
if (tag_exists(name))
    n->item = get_item_from_tag(name);
```
Reason:
The original logic did not account for the special case of the "__root__" node, leading to the incorrect assignment of the item for the root node. This oversight meant that the root node could potentially be linked incorrectly within the menu structure, causing errors in the menu's functionality.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
if (!strcmp(name, "__root__"))
    n->item = list_first_entry_or_null(&menu.master, struct item, master);
else
    n->item = get_item_from_tag(name);
```
Reason:
The fix introduces a conditional check specifically for the "__root__" node, ensuring that it is initialized correctly by linking it to the first entry in the master list. This differentiation allows the root node to be handled appropriately, preventing the errors that arose from the previous logic.

